When editing or testing `llm_demo`, read `llm_demo/ASSIGNMENT-2-IMPLEMENTATION-SPEC.md` first.

Key invariants:

- Keep exactly three control modes: `none`, `api`, `system`.
- Keep the same `user` prompt in every mode.
- `none`: same user message, sampling only.
- `api`: same user message plus `max_tokens`, `stop`, `response_format`, provider pin.
- `system`: system message plus same user message, no API control fields.
- Do not split API control into extra UI modes.
- Do not auto-fallback if OpenRouter returns 400 for `response_format`; show the error.
- Keep the LLM request as explicit REST through `httpx.post`, not an SDK.

Current working provider setup:

- Model: `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`
- API provider pin: `novita`
- `allow_fallbacks=false`
- `require_parameters=true`
- Demo prompt asks for 10 items; API/system constrain output to 5.
- API default `max_tokens=1600`; stop includes list item 6 and JSON key `"6"`.

Testing reminders:

- Use `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/private/tmp/aiadvent-pycache` for `py_compile` in Codex/macOS sandbox.
- Use `llm_demo/.venv/bin/python`, not bare system `python3`, to run the Flask app.
- Prefer no-network payload checks before real OpenRouter requests.
- Only run real 3-mode OpenRouter comparisons when the user permits spending the key.
